  <diagram id="mWffIyxM7jF6uQoUtA0H" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1981" dy="1546" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="cbAs7M2iqLtuT15kEG78-1" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span&gt;1. Questions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.3 – Fleet Pricing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Does the special daily price for Luxury vehicles apply to each physical vehicle or to a specific car model?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.7 – Corporate Customers:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can an authorized driver have more than one corporate company authorizing them at the same time?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.7 – Blacklist:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can a customer be blacklisted more than once, or can a blacklist record be removed or reversed?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.12 – Rentals:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can a rental be created for a corporate customer without selecting an authorized main driver?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.12 – Additional Drivers:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Are additional drivers required to be registered authorized drivers, or can other people be added?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.12 – Rentals:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can a rental have more than one extension directly, or is only one direct extension allowed?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.16 – Payments:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; How are monthly corporate invoices structured, and how are payments allocated to multiple rentals?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.15 – Maintenance:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Can one damage report result in a maintenance job that includes work beyond the reported damage?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="390" width="560" x="10" y="-280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cbAs7M2iqLtuT15kEG78-2" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span&gt;2. Assumptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.2 – Training:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; An additional &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;EnrollmentID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is used as the primary key for each course enrollment attempt because the SRS does not specify an attempt identifier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.3 – Fleet:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;ModelID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is introduced as a technical primary key for CAR_MODEL because the SRS does not specify a model identifier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.3 – Fleet Pricing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;SpecialDailyRate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is stored at the VEHICLE level for Luxury vehicles. This is a design assumption because the SRS does not specify whether special pricing belongs to a model or a physical vehicle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.3 – Category Rates:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;EffectiveFrom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is used with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;CategoryName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; as a composite primary key for CATEGORY_RATE.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.7 – Blacklist:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; A technical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;BlacklistID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is introduced as the primary key for each blacklist record because the SRS does not specify a record identifier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.7 – Corporate Drivers:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;DriverNo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is treated as a partial key within each corporate customer. The complete key is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;(CustomerNo, DriverNo)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.10 – Loyalty:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; A technical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;TransactionID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is introduced as the primary key for each loyalty transaction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.12 – Additional Drivers:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; A technical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;AdditionalDriverID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is introduced to identify each additional-driver record.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.15 – Suppliers:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; A technical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span&gt;SupplierID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span&gt; is introduced as the primary key because the SRS does not specify a supplier identifier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.16 – Corporate Invoices:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Invoice details are not fully specified in the SRS. Any invoice structure requires confirmation from Finance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="490" width="560" x="20" y="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cbAs7M2iqLtuT15kEG78-3" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span&gt;3. Contradictions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;No direct contradictions were identified between the SRS sections reviewed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;However, Section 7.16 mentions monthly invoices for corporate clients, while the payment requirements mainly describe payments associated with individual rental agreements. This is an unresolved design ambiguity rather than a confirmed contradiction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="560" x="26" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="vTN4YwFwCeaXRBeIH6GZ" name="4-Business-Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1030" dy="596" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="i-gFt6oAHwdcsXhXZvcN-1" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;Business Rules Beyond Constraints&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;span&gt;SRS Section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;span&gt;Business Rule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;span&gt;Why Constraints Are Not Enough&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;span&gt;How to Enforce It&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;A blacklisted customer cannot create a new reservation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;This rule requires checking another table before inserting a reservation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use a database trigger or stored procedure to check the customer&#39;s blacklist status before creating a reservation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;A vehicle cannot be transferred to the same branch where it is currently located.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;The rule requires checking the vehicle&#39;s current location and previous transfer records.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use a stored procedure or trigger to validate the vehicle&#39;s current branch before recording a transfer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Loyalty points must be recorded for every earning or redemption transaction, and the customer&#39;s tier must reflect the total points balance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;This requires maintaining a transaction history and calculating an aggregate balance across multiple records.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use application logic or database procedures to record point movements and calculate the customer&#39;s tier.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 7.12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;A corporate rental&#39;s main driver must be an authorized driver belonging to the same corporate customer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;This requires checking the relationship between the rental&#39;s customer and the selected authorized driver across multiple tables.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use a stored procedure or application logic to validate the driver before creating the rental.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="470" width="560" x="30" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
